# HTTP API Conventions

- Use ASP.NET Core Controllers rather than Minimal APIs.
- Controllers inherit from `ControllerBase`.
- Use `[ApiController]`.
- Use attribute routing with `[HttpGet]`, `[HttpPost]`, `[HttpDelete]`, etc.
- Prefer typed `ActionResult<T>` responses when applicable.
- Expose meaningful response types/status codes through OpenAPI metadata.
- Keep business rules out of controllers.
- Async HTTP operations should accept `CancellationToken` when appropriate.
- Before introducing a new controller pattern, inspect an existing controller and follow the established convention.